 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 542169,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The figure shows a map of the Island of Oahu in the State of Hawaii divided into regions. Draw a graph in which each vertex represents one of the regions and each edge represents a shared land border.\n<figure>\n<figcaption>Map of Oahu</figcaption>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/b5c7e5db065abc62.png\" alt=\"A map shows the regions of Oahu. The regions are North Shore, Leeward Coast, Central, Windward Coast, and South.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Draw a vertex to represent each region. Label each with the initial of the region (N for North Shore, L for Leeward Coast, C for Central, S for South, and W for Windward Coast). Draw edges to connect vertices that share a common border. The North Shore region shares a border with Leeward Coast, Central, and Windward Coast, so draw an edge from N to L, C, and W.</p>\n<p>Leeward Coast shares a border with North Shore and Central. You already have the edge between N and L, so all you need to add is the edge between N and C.</p>\n<p>Central shares a border with all the other four regions. You need to add an edge to W and S.</p>\n<p>Windward shares a border with North Shore, Central, and South. You already have the edge to N and C, so add the edge to S.</p>\n<p>South shares a border with Central and Windward. You already have both of those. You are done.</p>\n<p>Go back over your drawing and the map. Count the degree of your vertices and compare it to the “degree” of each region on the map.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<figure><figcaption>Graph Representing Common Boundaries Between Regions of Oahu</figcaption>\n<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBaTBMIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--48fa03cc3932f1be4ed0a4499c3a303e2cf1dcc6/CS_Figure_12_01_015.png\" alt=\"A graph represents common boundaries between regions of Oahu. The five vertices are L, N, W, C, and S. Edges connect L with N and C. Edges connect N with W and C. Edges connect W with C and S. An edge connects S with C.\"></figure>"
    }
   ],
